<statement>
<p>
	This program combines all the helper functions written above and in the previous assignment to implement a fully working Tic-Tac-Toe game.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>This script should have three main parts:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Game Setup.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>his section handles the following tasks:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell>
			<p>
				<ul>
					<li>Close any open figures.</li>
					<li>Create the initial game_state structure with all of the default values.</li>
					<li>Ask the user what type of game will be played. Here are the options: Player vs Player (PVP) Player vs Environment (PVE) Environment vs Environment (EVE)</li>
					<li>If PVE is selected, your script should ask the user for the AI level. Here are the level options: <pf>'1'</pf> - use your <pf>dumb_ai_move</pf> code. <pf>'2'</pf> - use your <pf>better_ai_move</pf> code. <pf>'3'</pf> - use your <pf>my_ai_move</pf> code.</li>
					<li>If EVE is selected, your script should ask the user for both AI levels. The options are the same as in the PVE version.</li>
					<li>Display the initial game interface.</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Ask your questions using MATLAB's</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>questdlg</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>command. Type</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>doc questdlg</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>into the command window to see an example of its use.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Game Loop.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>his section calls your</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>game_loop</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>code corresponding to the selected version of Tic-Tac-Toe in the Game Setup.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Results.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>This section displays the game's results in the game interface's</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>title</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Once completed, this program should play a complete game of tic-tac-toe.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Copy and paste all helper functions called by this script at the bottom of this script. Include any functions that are also called from within the helper functions. The order in which you place them does not matter as long as they are all below the script commands.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>In your final submission (within your</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>display_initial_board</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>code), do the following:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell>
			<p>
				<ul>
					<li>Set <pf>grid off</pf> to <pf>grid on</pf></li>
					<li>Add the following lines of code to turn off the x and y axis: <pf> ax = gca; ax.XColor = 'none'; ax.YColor = 'none'; </pf></li>
				</ul>
			</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
